{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_17\">Problem 17</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 17\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/057ef0b09e7b2a7d366a6950fafc9d9ca9a7510d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91ab8804f865d1c887d9ee444361176911795461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4dfafa4192cacd28dd2711192b22ae68a3770f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec6916b50feec24773d374eaada26a95bcabc6fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9988fbe7f7b42a0b56481882dfc4e08246d9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ST$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b74d37f332a044f3c256f68d13e107c25ab50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QS=SU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14a56a5cf2170129b5f8c1d0b69b90617cb4c895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UT=TR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />. The perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec30be26c21a38544a25e260c357dc9645017a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PST$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874e186169fbede334a8100b3b9860f9d40642f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;mathptmx&quot;);  defaultpen(TimesRoman()); import markers; defaultpen(linewidth(1bp)); size(150);  frame twoSticks = stickframe(n=2, size=1.4mm, space=(0.6mm,0));  real k1 = 267/697; real k2 = 97/389; real PQR = acos((18^2-19^2-17^2)/(-2*19*17)); real PRQ = acos((19^2-18^2-17^2)/(-2*18*17));  pair P = (19*cos(PQR),19*sin(PQR)); pair Q = (0,0); pair R = (17,0); pair SPoint = (19*k1*cos(PQR),19*k1*sin(PQR)); pair T = (17+18*k2*cos(pi-PRQ),18*k2*sin(pi-PRQ)); pair U = intersectionpoint(arc(SPoint,19*k1,180,360), SPoint--T, -1);   draw((P--Q--R--cycle));  draw(Q--U--R); draw(Q--SPoint, marker(markinterval(1, twoSticks, rotated=true), true)); draw(SPoint--U, marker(markinterval(1, twoSticks, rotated=true), true)); draw(U--T, marker(markinterval(stickframe(n=1, 1.4mm), true))); draw(T--R, marker(markinterval(stickframe(n=1, 1.4mm), true)));  label(&quot;$S$&quot;, SPoint, W); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;, Q, SW); label(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, N); label(&quot;$R$&quot;, R, SE); label(&quot;$T$&quot;, T, E); label(&quot;$U$&quot;, U, N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad81a862e612c85318f98179518a0f400cf91f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   36  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   35  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   37  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   34  \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   38  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"430\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To calculate the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec30be26c21a38544a25e260c357dc9645017a1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PST$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, we must find the sum of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805452ee372321839953fbd750cd9b23b973a3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9988fbe7f7b42a0b56481882dfc4e08246d9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ST$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbec66fb59a93b6cfa2470238cbdddb55244aaef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TR$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />. Using the equalities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b74d37f332a044f3c256f68d13e107c25ab50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QS=SU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/a/14a56a5cf2170129b5f8c1d0b69b90617cb4c895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UT=TR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />, we can notice that the perimeter is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c2d4929034f816537d7f94640b52f0146834b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ + PR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />. Specifically, we can break <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/9/3e9988fbe7f7b42a0b56481882dfc4e08246d9d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ST$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> into segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/7161ae1acdc5487ce73900726f6a41cd57973ccc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/57773a22666a2a3855c7116b2a5f880ca160d09d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$UT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, which have the same length as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da1bd2309dd6ebab80a9ada0c1cd7568ff5a30e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"26\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbec66fb59a93b6cfa2470238cbdddb55244aaef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TR$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, respectively. Thus, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\tPS + ST + TP &amp;= PS + (SU + UT) + TP\\\\\n\t&amp;= PS + (QS + TR) + TP\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nUsing the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b71e69adc1445aed1d5069f8a8ba4ccda937240b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS + QS = PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2e705ce65f3af4d18fed012cba50a389fb6d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TR + TP = PR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />, this becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1c9589327f00d2c92bef8765202e49329b7b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ + PR =  19 + 17 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"252\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a